WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.890
On February 2, 2010 the U.S.
Treasury estimated the

00:04.890 --> 00:11.900
national debt at 1.2278 times
10 to the 13th power.

00:11.900 --> 00:15.930
And just to get a sense of
things, 1 times 10 to the

00:15.930 --> 00:19.330
sixth is a million, 1 times 10
to the ninth is a billion, 1

00:19.330 --> 00:21.470
times 10 to the 12th
is a trillion.

00:21.470 --> 00:23.450
So we're talking on the
order of magnitude

00:23.450 --> 00:25.210
of 10 trillion dollars.

00:25.210 --> 00:28.470
So this is about 12
trillion dollars.

00:28.470 --> 00:31.970
Then they tell us that the U.S.
Census Bureau's estimate

00:31.970 --> 00:36.390
for the U.S. population was
about 3.086 times 10 to the

00:36.390 --> 00:37.100
eighth power.

00:37.100 --> 00:39.875
So this is a little over
300 million people.

00:39.875 --> 00:41.900
So that's an interesting number
right there, it's the

00:41.900 --> 00:42.870
population.

00:42.870 --> 00:46.510
And then they say, using these
estimates calculate the

00:46.510 --> 00:49.400
per-person share of
the national debt.

00:49.400 --> 00:51.840
So essentially, we want to
take the entire debt and

00:51.840 --> 00:53.450
divide by the number
of people.

00:53.450 --> 00:56.850
That'll give us the per-person
share of the national debt.

00:56.850 --> 01:00.320
Use scientific notation to make
your calculations and

01:00.320 --> 01:01.630
express your answer in both

01:01.630 --> 01:05.710
scientific and decimal notation.

01:05.710 --> 01:07.860
Which means just as
a regular number.

01:07.860 --> 01:11.410
Round to four decimal places
while making calculations.

01:11.410 --> 01:12.990
So we want the per-person
debt.

01:12.990 --> 01:14.430
So we want to take the total
debt and divide by

01:14.430 --> 01:16.050
the number of people.

01:16.050 --> 01:26.270
So the total debt is 1.2278
times 10 to the 13th.

01:26.270 --> 01:31.610
And we want to divide that by
the total number of people,

01:31.610 --> 01:37.660
which is 3.086 times
10 to the eighth.

01:37.660 --> 01:40.160
And we could separate this into
two division problems. We

01:40.160 --> 01:45.070
could say that this is equal
to the division right here,

01:45.070 --> 01:56.310
1.2278 divided by 3.086.

01:56.310 --> 02:02.630
And then times 10 to the 13th
divided by 10 to the eighth.

02:02.630 --> 02:05.280
Now, what's 10 to the 13th
divided by 10 to the eighth?

02:05.280 --> 02:06.530
Let me do it over here.

02:06.578 --> 02:13.590
The way I think about it, this
is the exact same thing as 10

02:13.590 --> 02:18.860
to the 13th times 10 to
the negative eight.

02:18.860 --> 02:20.530
This is an eight right here.

02:20.530 --> 02:22.610
If you have a 10 to the eighth
in the denominator, that's

02:22.610 --> 02:24.870
like multiplying by 10 to
the negative eight.

02:24.870 --> 02:28.660
So you have 13, you the same
base 10, so 10 to the 13th

02:28.660 --> 02:31.770
times 10 to the negative eight
is going to be 10 to

02:31.770 --> 02:33.390
the 13 minus 8.

02:33.390 --> 02:35.070
Which is 10 to the fifth.

02:35.070 --> 02:38.910
Or another way to think about
it: If you have the base in

02:38.910 --> 02:40.880
the denominator, you subtract
the exponents.

02:40.880 --> 02:42.190
So it's 13 minus 8.

02:42.190 --> 02:43.420
10 to the fifth.

02:43.420 --> 02:52.360
So it's this blue expression
times 10 to the fifth.

02:52.360 --> 02:57.240
And let's get a calculator out
to calculate this right here.

02:57.240 --> 02:59.985
And they say round everything
to four decimal places, so

02:59.985 --> 03:02.550
I'll keep that in mind.

03:02.550 --> 03:03.720
Let me turn my calculator on.

03:03.720 --> 03:22.760
1.2278 divided by 3.086
is equal to 0.3979.

03:22.760 --> 03:26.020
Because we want to round
right there.

03:26.020 --> 03:27.005
Let me remember that.

03:27.005 --> 03:30.780
Or let me just put it
on the side so I can

03:30.780 --> 03:33.020
still look at it.

03:33.020 --> 03:35.810
So this this little
dividing decimals

03:35.810 --> 03:44.840
problem results in 0.3979.

03:44.840 --> 03:51.510
And of course, times 10 to the
fifth dollars per person.

03:51.510 --> 03:53.640
Once again, you might be tempted
to say, hey this is in

03:53.640 --> 03:54.590
scientific notation.

03:54.590 --> 03:57.760
I have some number times
a power of ten.

03:57.760 --> 04:01.250
But notice, this number is not
greater than or equal to 1.

04:01.250 --> 04:03.010
Remember, this number, if you
want to be formal about

04:03.010 --> 04:06.260
scientific notation, has to be
greater than or equal to 1, or

04:06.260 --> 04:07.770
less than 10.

04:07.770 --> 04:12.020
So what we can do here
is we can multiply.

04:12.020 --> 04:14.580
If we don't want to change the
number, we can multiply this

04:14.580 --> 04:17.630
number by 10 and divide
this number by 10.

04:17.630 --> 04:20.209
Or another way you can think
about it is, this whole thing

04:20.209 --> 04:26.180
can be rewritten as
0.3979 times 10

04:26.180 --> 04:30.110
times 10 to the fourth.

04:30.110 --> 04:32.510
What I did was just now was I
broke up the 10 of the fifth

04:32.510 --> 04:35.710
into a 10 and a 10
to the fourth.

04:35.710 --> 04:38.120
And I did that because I want
to multiply this by 10 so I

04:38.120 --> 04:41.250
can get a 3 out front
instead of a 0.3.

04:41.250 --> 04:44.370
So let's do that.

04:44.370 --> 04:46.400
So essentially, I took a 10 out
of the 10 to the fifth.

04:46.400 --> 04:48.690
I divided it by 10, I multiplied
this other guy by

04:48.690 --> 04:50.670
10, not changing the
whole number.

04:50.670 --> 04:57.840
So then this right here will
become 3.979 and then times 10

04:57.840 --> 04:59.090
to the fourth.

05:03.140 --> 05:05.630
So that's how much debt
there is per-person

05:05.630 --> 05:07.140
in scientific notation.

05:07.140 --> 05:09.460
So this is debt per person in scientific notation.

05:09.460 --> 05:15.240
Now, in the problem they also
wanted us to express it in

05:15.240 --> 05:17.700
decimal notation.

05:17.700 --> 05:20.420
Which is just kind of standard
writing it as a number with

05:20.420 --> 05:23.080
our standard numeric
decimal system.

05:23.080 --> 05:26.100
So what is 3.979 times
10 to the fourth?

05:26.100 --> 05:27.350
Let's think about it.

05:27.350 --> 05:33.490
We have 3.979 times ten to the fourth.

05:33.490 --> 05:36.830
Well let me just
do it this way.

05:36.830 --> 05:38.670
Let's just move the
decimal space.

05:38.670 --> 05:41.910
If we multiply it by 10, we're
going to get 39.79.

05:41.910 --> 05:43.590
If we multiply it by
10 squared, we're

05:43.590 --> 05:45.335
going to get 397.9.

05:45.335 --> 05:47.250
If we multiply it by 10
to the third, we're

05:47.250 --> 05:49.655
going to get 3,979.

05:49.655 --> 05:53.020
If we multiply it by 10 to the
fourth, we're going to get one

05:53.020 --> 05:54.340
more zero right there.

05:54.340 --> 05:55.320
So we're essentially
going to move the

05:55.320 --> 05:56.680
decimal four to the right.

05:56.738 --> 06:00.950
So I could write it like this.

06:00.950 --> 06:06.620
This is equal to $39,790.

06:06.620 --> 06:09.000
So if you think about the
national debt per person.

06:09.000 --> 06:13.070
Every man, woman, and child in
the United States essentially

06:13.070 --> 06:21.267
owes $39,790.
